# sepolicy.rule — SELinux rules applied at boot by the Tanuki engine
# (magiskinit time), one statement per line. Lines starting with '#' are
# skipped. An empty file is removed by tanuki.sh and never installed.
#
# Reference: https://topjohnwu.github.io/Magisk/guides.html
#
# Example: allow the module's own service domain to read a directory
# allow my_domain my_file_type:dir { open read search };
